tools.description:
List pods in a namespace (kubectl get pods on the selected machine).

No capabilities.kubectl gate — failures surface via exitCode; use context_probe for CLI presence.
Example: {"namespace":"default","labelSelector":"app=web","output":"wide"}

Run a command inside a pod container (kubectl exec on the selected machine, non-interactive).

When to use: scripts, env, dirs inside a container. Not file logs (remote_read_file) or container stdout history (k8s_logs).
Example: {"namespace":"dev","pod":"web-abc","command":"ls -la /app","container":"app"}

Fetch pod container stdout/stderr (kubectl logs on the selected machine).

When to use: container runtime logs. Not log files on disk (remote_read_file). Often empty for sshd-only idle pods.
Example: {"namespace":"dev","pod":"web-abc","tail":200,"since":"1h"}

Probe docker/kubectl CLI on the selected machine. SSH success ≠ docker/kubectl.

Returns true | false | unknown. Prefer this (or let docker_* auto-probe) before assuming docker.
Example: {} or {"host":"10.0.0.5"}

Start an async copy job (same rules as remote_copy_file) and return transferId immediately.

Prefer when size>256MB or ETA>2min. Poll remote_copy_status; cancel with remote_copy_cancel.
Example: {"source":{"target":"remote","path":"/tmp/big.pt"},"dest":{"target":"local","path":"C:/data/big.pt"},"skipIfComplete":true,"totalTimeoutMs":7200000}

Poll async copy job status by transferId from remote_copy_start.

Returns status (queued|running|success|failed|cancelled|timeout) and progress bytes/percent/speed/eta.
Example: {"transferId":"copy-xxx"}
